CORE
main.c

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 14 SHOULD FAIL: out havocked: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
inline assembly not understood \(unsupported directive '.*'\); approximating it by havocking
--
--
An asm statement that is not understood is approximated: its outputs are
havocked and the conservative approximation is reported with a warning, so a
property depending on the asm's effect is no longer falsely proven.
